    {
      "id": "mt6n57vqx6h3id",
      "name": "Bump Digital",
      "notes": "",
      "createdAt": 1787539969574,
      "context": "Bump Digital is the agency Kelsey contracts with; she runs Meta (and proposed LinkedIn) ads for their client Plumbline. KAM contact: Josh Blackman, josh.blackman@bumpdigital.co.nz, 021 840 017.\n\nPLUMBLINE (end client): Bathware/tapware brand, NZ + AU. plumbline.co.nz. Contact: Lauren Rogers, Lauren.rogers@plumbline.co.nz. Existing Google Ads advertiser. New catalogue launches annually (seasonality factor).\n\nBRAND: Pillars = Design, Quality, Choice. B2B pitch (specifiers/architects): design-led product backed by technical resources (3D files, renders, compliance) that keeps projects moving instead of stalling at spec stage. B2C pitch (homeowners): quality bathware that's already resolved (finish, function, durability). Credibility: Lead Free Tapware, Designed in NZ, Manufactured in NZ, Toitu Certified, most complete architectural bathware collection. Competitors: Robertsons Bathware, Elementi, ABI Interiors, Astra Walker, Newtech Bathroomware, Caroma, Duravit, Methven, St Michel Bathroomware, Nero, Bath Co. Full brand guidelines held by Lauren, share on request.\n\nMETA ADS - CURRENT STATE (Bump Digital's review): 7 campaigns live at $150/day; only 'Book a Consultation - Melbourne' ($50/day) is actionable/lead-generating. The other $100/day (2/3 of spend) is pure brand awareness with no measurable objective - the core inefficiency flagged.\n\nMETA ADS - PROPOSED GROWTH PLAN: Restructure to $140/day, 100% actionable, across 5 locations (Melbourne/Auckland/Wellington showrooms + NZ & AU national), split B2B (trade/specifiers) vs B2C (homeowners). Showroom 'Book a Consultation' campaigns: $20/day each x3 = $60/day. National product/catalogue campaigns (ecommerce + lead capture): NZ $40/day + AU $40/day = $80/day. Creative needed: Auckland + Wellington showroom graphics, catalogue graphics x8, optional showroom video walkthroughs. Management scope: 7 hrs one-time setup, then 7 hrs/month ongoing (5 management, 1 creative brief, 1 reporting).\n\nLINKEDIN - PROPOSED LAUNCH (new channel, B2B/specifiers): Reuse showroom creative + text-only ads. $60/day (~$1,800/month): 3x consultation campaigns ($10/day each - Melbourne/Wellington/Auckland) + 2x catalogue campaigns ($15/day each - NZ/AU). Setup 6 hrs, then 6 hrs/month ongoing (3 management, 2 creative, 1 reporting).\n\nCOMBINED (Meta+LinkedIn): 26 hrs first month with setup, 13 hrs every month after.\n\nCONVERSIONS THAT COUNT: showroom visits, phone calls, ecommerce sales, retail sales, in-person presentations, A&D spec/CAD/sample requests, catalogue requests, quote requests, EDM sign-ups.\n\nEMAIL MARKETING: Not in Bump Digital's initial scope, but Plumbline said yes to wanting help with it (esp. driving ecommerce sales) - a flagged upsell opportunity.\n\nPLUMBLINE'S OWN FY27 MARKETING PLAN (background, not Kelsey's scope): Theme 'Demanding Outcomes'. Audiences: Specifiers (hero focus, 'Win The Specifier'), Homeowners (affluent/designer-led), Retailers (opportunistic). Big projects: Future Website, Catalogue 26/27, AU Market Expansion, Strong Brand in Retail, Lead-Focused Marketing, Product Configurator. Total FY27 media budget: NZ $284K + AU $126K = $410K NZD, across Digital/Social, Print & Editorial, and Partnerships & Events. Plumbline's NZ budget includes a line for 'Bump Digital / Admin - digital management & production fees' at $8,400/yr.\n\n(Sourced from docs Kelsey shared directly in chat on 2026-09-07: Bump Digital onboarding brief, Bump Digital's Plumbline Meta/LinkedIn proposal, and Plumbline's FY27 marketing plans (Overall + Australia). Full documents are not in this export - ask Kelsey if anything beyond this summary is needed.)"
    }
